xnu 0378: give Photos the UI hook without a probe file

Measured 2026-11-19: with the CGImage-to-surface bridge installed, Photos draws
its Library tile and opens the viewer on the imported picture; without it the
tile is black. The bridge itself is now installed on every launch of
MobileSlideShow (tools/mondrian-ui-hook.m), but the app only receives the dylib
while /private/var/vm/mondrian-probe exists, so a default boot still shows a
black tile.

Add bit 8 (0x100) to the hook mask for MobileSlideShow and match the last path
component, the same rule the probe names use. The probe bit keeps priority when
mondrian-probe is present. boards.py carries 6 | 0x100 = 262.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index cdedd47..ff7180b 100755
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5651,6 +5651,15 @@ bad:
  * none of them is a UI process. A default boot injects nothing new.
  */
 #define MONDRIAN_HOOK_PROBE             0x80
+/*
+ * Photos (MobileSlideShow) is the one app whose picture path needs the hook:
+ * the CGImage-to-surface bridge is what makes its Library tiles and its viewer
+ * draw (measured 2026-11-19), and the app enables multi-library mode itself,
+ * which the hook has to observe rather than block. Unlike the probe names
+ * above, this bit is part of the default mask: the working state must not
+ * depend on a file in /private/var/vm.
+ */
+#define MONDRIAN_HOOK_PHOTOS            0x100
 
 /*
  * Does this boot's copy of a dylib exist in /private/var/vm? glblob=1 writes
@@ -5784,6 +5793,28 @@ mondrian_probe_app_env(struct image_params *imgp, char *env, size_t size)
 	return true;
 }
 
+/*
+ * An app does not exec under its bare name: measured 2026-11-19, MobileSlideShow
+ * arrives as /Applications/MobileSlideShow.app/MobileSlideShow while SpringBoard
+ * and the poster extensions arrive plain. Compare the last path component, the
+ * same rule mondrian_probe_target() already uses for the probe names.
+ */
+static bool
+mondrian_name_is(const char *name, size_t len, const char *want)
+{
+	const char *base = name;
+	size_t wantlen = strlen(want);
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
+		if (name[i] == '/') {
+			base = name + i + 1;
+		}
+	}
+	return (size_t)(name + len - base) == wantlen &&
+	    strncmp(base, want, wantlen) == 0;
+}
